{"t": 1794107650.388578, "kind": "call", "tool": "gitlab_create_merge_request_thread", "args": {"body": "**Main pipeline #8812 is red \u2014 root cause and fix**\n\nFailing job: `test:contract` (`contract/test_invoice.py::test_invoice_number_format`)\n\n```\nAssertionError: assert 'INV-2026-42' == 'INV-2026-000042'\n```\n\nRoot cause: `billing/invoice.py::invoice_number()` still emitted the raw sequence (`INV-2026-42`). The ERP v2 contract (FIN-77) requires the sequence part to be zero-padded to 6 digits, i.e. `INV-2026-000042`. The contract test reached `main` ahead of the implementation, so `main` went red while the code was still producing the old v1-style number.\n\nFix in `billing/invoice.py`:\n\n```python\nreturn f\"INV-{year}-{seq:06d}\"\n```\n\nThe `INV-<year>-` prefix is unchanged and sequences of 7+ digits are still rendered in full (no truncation). The contract test was not touched \u2014 it encodes the ERP v2 requirement, so the code was the thing that had to change.\n\nVerified locally against the contract assertion (plus 0 / 7 / 999999 / 1234567 edge cases): all pass. `lint` was already green, so `test:contract` was the only blocker.", "merge_request_iid": "12", "project_id": "acme/billing-legacy"}, "ok": true}
